<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins Czech turbine deal.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins Czech turbine deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>GEC-Alsthom said its European Gas Turbine (EGT) unit had won a 16 million ecu deal for equipment for a cogeneration plant, including a 70 megawatt (MW) gas turbine, in the Czech Republic.</p>
<p>The turbine will be delivered in the spring of 1998.</p>
<p>The deal was awarded by Noell-KCR Energie und Umwelttechnik GmbH which is lead contractor for the power plant at Usti.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture between General Electric Co Plc of Britain and Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
</text>
